Z||000000||qwikgta||05-14-2001||10:29 PM||||I am putting a header on my 2.5L and when I installed the header it hits the A/C compresser.  I modified the rear bracket which was in the way and after I tryed to install the header it turns out that the header will still hit the compresser.  Can I remove the A/C and run a non-A/C belt on the car.  Will I have any probs with this.  I want the header and I don't use the A/C anyway.<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||5
Z||000001||cadaver||05-14-2001||11:27 PM||||I dont think it would be a problem as long as it doesnt use the compressor to tension the belt. But I would rather just make it work if it were my car.||||reg||1
